Actual package setup in this cloud instance (Debian 13, amd64):
APT_CONFIG=/workspace/tooling/apt/apt.conf /usr/bin/apt-get update
cd /workspace/tooling/ghdl
APT_CONFIG=/workspace/tooling/apt/apt.conf /usr/bin/apt-get download ghdl-mcode ghdl-common libgnat-14
for package in *.deb; do dpkg-deb -x "$package" root; done
cd /workspace/tooling/gui
APT_CONFIG=/workspace/tooling/apt/apt.conf /usr/bin/apt-get download gtkwave xvfb libjudydebian1 x11-apps libxcb-damage0
for package in *.deb; do dpkg-deb -x "$package" root; done
glib-compile-schemas /workspace/tooling/gui/root/usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas

APT used https://deb.debian.org/debian trixie main with
signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg.
No signature, checksum, or TLS checks were disabled.
matplotlib and ImageMagick were already installed.
The GHDL wrapper sets local LD_LIBRARY_PATH and GHDL_PREFIX.
The GTKWave screenshot helper sets local LD_LIBRARY_PATH and GSETTINGS_SCHEMA_DIR,
starts Xvfb without TCP listeners and captures the real display with ImageMagick.
It requires permission to bind a local Unix socket, unavailable in the default sandbox.
